# Convai docs tooling.
#
# .convai-docs/rules/ IS committed: it is the rule bundle that Codex CLI and Cursor read,
# generated from the convai-docs plugin by scripts/sync_agent_rules.py. Everyone needs it,
# so it must not be ignored.
#
# Everything else under .convai-docs/ is a per-person working artifact that is never
# published and never appears in SUMMARY.md.
.convai-docs/*
!.convai-docs/rules/

# The site-check baseline IS committed. It records the findings that already existed
# when the whole-repository check was adopted, so only new problems fail a pull request.
# Leaving it untracked would make the check report every one of them on every run, and a
# check that is red on day one is one people learn to scroll past.
!.convai-docs/site-baseline.json

# The retiring-sections list IS committed, for the same reason: check_site.py reads it to
# decide which findings belong to content awaiting deletion. Untracked, the check counts
# those sections as live and every run reports work nobody intends to do.
!.convai-docs/retiring-sections.txt

# Python bytecode from running the structure linter
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]

# Editor / OS noise
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
*.swp
